  "uncertain": [
    "Label choice for ATmega pins: AVR port names (PB5, PC0...) treated as port names rather than GPIO names; Arduino names (D13, A0/D14) used as labels.",
    "Qwiic pin-to-wire mapping inferred from the colored callout lines converging on the small connector photo."
  ],
  "notes": "SparkFun RedBoard Plus DEV-18158 pinout. White 'Name' boxes (silkscreen) placed first in functions when different; Arduino names used as labels. 'Reset' is printed with an overline (active-low), recorded as 'Reset'. Qwiic pin order traced from the colored callout wires (black, red, blue, yellow from left to right on the connector). USB pads come from the back-of-board inset (rule 1: individually labeled). The A4/A5 cut-jumper inset was not transcribed."
